---
import core from '../../../lib/relational-collection/core.json';
const rows=[...core.orders,{order_id:105,customer_id:1,placed_at:'2026-10-21T12:00:00Z',status:'pending'},{order_id:106,customer_id:3,placed_at:'2026-10-21T12:00:00Z',status:'pending'}].map((row,page)=>({...row,location:`(${page},1)`}));
---
<figure class="key-figure" data-key-order data-rows={JSON.stringify(rows)} aria-labelledby="r10-key-title">
 <figcaption id="r10-key-title"><span>Figure 2</span> Which entries must the search pass?</figcaption>
 <p class="question">Customer 1’s two newest orders since 15 October:<br/><code>ORDER BY placed_at DESC, order_id DESC LIMIT 2</code></p>
 <label>Index key <select data-key><option value="customer">Customer only</option><option value="history" selected>Customer, then newest</option><option value="date">Newest across customers</option></select></label><p class="key-code" data-key-label data-live></p>
 <div class="key-layout"><div><p class="panel-label">Index · key → row location</p><ol data-entries></ol></div><div class="table-work"><p class="panel-label">Table rows fetched</p><ol data-fetched data-live></ol><p class="panel-label">Answer · newest first</p><ol data-answer data-live></ol></div></div>
 <p class="work-count" data-count data-live></p><p data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite"></p>
 <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Figure 2 controls"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step></span><div data-hold><span></span></div></div>
 <details><summary>Read this comparison as text</summary><p>The customer-only index stores customer IDs and row locations. Reading its three customer-1 entries fetches orders 101, 103 and 105 from the table; only those fetches reveal their dates, order IDs and status. Order 101 is too old. Sort the other two to return 105, then 103. The history key already stores customer, date and order ID: it reads 105, then 103 and fetches those two rows for status. The date-first key reads 106, 105 and 103, but rejects Edda’s 106 using its indexed customer ID, fetching only the two matching rows. All three routes return 105, then 103.</p></details>
 <p class="caption">A conceptual entry walk over the core orders plus later illustrative orders 105 and 106. Locations are invented (page, item) pairs, continuing Figure 1; equal customer-only keys are shown in locator order. Dates and IDs appear in an entry only when its key contains them. Both later orders are pending, with no new lines or payments. This is not a native plan for five rows.</p>
</figure>
<script>
 import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-key-order]').forEach(root=>{
 const rows=JSON.parse(root.dataset.rows!);const select=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-key]')!;
 const displayDate=(value:string)=>new Date(value).toLocaleDateString('en-GB',{day:'numeric',month:'short',timeZone:'UTC'});
 const qualifies=(r:any)=>r.customer_id===1&&r.placed_at>='2026-10-15';
 const byNewest=(a:any,b:any)=>b.placed_at.localeCompare(a.placed_at)||b.order_id-a.order_id;
 const sorted=()=>[...rows].sort(select.value==='customer'?((a,b)=>a.customer_id-b.customer_id||rows.indexOf(a)-rows.indexOf(b)):select.value==='history'?((a,b)=>a.customer_id-b.customer_id||byNewest(a,b)):byNewest);
 const visited=()=>select.value==='customer'?sorted().filter(x=>x.customer_id===1):select.value==='history'?sorted().filter(x=>x.customer_id===1).slice(0,2):sorted().slice(0,3);
 const draw=(step:number)=>{
 const mode=select.value,path=visited(),seen=path.slice(0,step),complete=step===path.length;
 const fetched=mode==='customer'?seen:seen.filter(qualifies);
 const answer=seen.filter(qualifies).sort(byNewest).slice(0,2);
 root.querySelector('[data-key-label]')!.textContent=({customer:'(customer_id)',history:'(customer_id, placed_at DESC, order_id DESC)',date:'(placed_at DESC, order_id DESC, customer_id)'})[mode];
 root.querySelector('[data-entries]')!.innerHTML=sorted().map(r=>{
 const read=seen.some(x=>x.order_id===r.order_id);
 const key=mode==='customer'?`customer ${r.customer_id}`:mode==='history'?`customer ${r.customer_id} · ${displayDate(r.placed_at)} · ID ${r.order_id}`:`${displayDate(r.placed_at)} · ID ${r.order_id} · customer ${r.customer_id}`;
 return `<li class="${read?'read':''}"><span>${key}</span><small>→ ${r.location}${read?' · read':''}</small></li>`;
 }).join('');
 root.querySelector('[data-fetched]')!.innerHTML=fetched.length?fetched.map(r=>`<li><span>${r.location} → order ${r.order_id}</span><small>${displayDate(r.placed_at)} · ${r.status}${qualifies(r)?' · qualifies':' · before cutoff'}</small></li>`).join(''):'<li>No rows fetched yet.</li>';
 root.querySelector('[data-answer]')!.innerHTML=(mode==='customer'&&!complete?[]:answer).map(r=>`<li>Order ${r.order_id} · ${displayDate(r.placed_at)}</li>`).join('')||(mode==='customer'&&!complete?'<li>Check all customer-1 rows before sorting.</li>':'<li>No matches yet.</li>');
 root.querySelector('[data-count]')!.textContent=`${seen.length} ${seen.length===1?'entry':'entries'} read · ${fetched.length} table ${fetched.length===1?'row':'rows'} fetched${complete&&mode==='customer'?' · sort needed':complete?' · 2 matches, stop; no sort':''}`;
 root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=step===0?(mode==='customer'?'Find customer 1. Only customer IDs and locations are in these entries. Fetch each row to learn its date.':mode==='history'?'Find customer 1’s newest entry. The key gives the date and order ID; fetch the row for status.':'Start at the newest entry across all customers. Use the indexed customer ID to reject other customers before fetching.'):
 complete?(mode==='customer'?'All three rows have been fetched. 101 is too old; sort the survivors to return 105, then 103.':mode==='history'?'105 and 103 qualify. Both rows supply status; no later entry can displace them.':'106 belongs to customer 3: skip its table row. Fetch 105 and 103 for status; they complete the answer.'):
 mode==='customer'?`Fetch ${path[step-1].location}: it is order ${path[step-1].order_id}, dated ${displayDate(path[step-1].placed_at)}. ${qualifies(path[step-1])?'It qualifies; other customer-1 rows may still be newer.':'It is before the cutoff.'}`:
 qualifies(path[step-1])?`The key for order ${path[step-1].order_id} qualifies. Fetch its row for status.`:`The newest key is ID 106, ahead of same-time 105. Customer 3 fails the condition; no table fetch.`;
 };
 const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>visited().length+1,draw});select.addEventListener('change',()=>{player.render();root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reset]')!.click();});
 });
</script>
<style>
 .key-figure{padding:1rem;margin:2rem 0;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface-alt);font:.9rem/1.5 var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font:1.2rem var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:1rem}figcaption span{font:.75rem var(--font-sans);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.7rem}.question{font-size:.9rem}.key-code{font:.8rem/1.5 var(--font-mono);overflow-wrap:anywhere}.key-layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr;gap:1.25rem;margin:1rem 0}.panel-label{font-weight:600}ol{list-style:none;padding:0}.key-figure :global(li){display:grid;gap:.2rem;padding:.5rem;margin:.4rem 0;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface);font-size:.8rem}.key-figure :global(li small){color:var(--color-text-secondary);font-size:.75rem}.key-figure :global(li.read){outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:-2px}.table-work{min-height:10rem}.work-count{font-weight:600}select{display:block;max-width:100%;font:inherit;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);padding:.5rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);margin-top:.4rem}.controls{display:flex;gap:.5rem;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap}button{font:inherit;padding:.45rem .65rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);border-radius:.25rem;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);cursor:pointer}button[aria-disabled=true]{opacity:.5}button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px}[data-explanation]{min-height:4.5em;border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding-left:.8rem}[data-hold]{height:3px;width:100%;background:var(--color-rule)}[data-hold] span{height:100%;display:block;background:var(--color-accent);width:0}.caption{font-size:.82rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}details{margin-top:1rem}summary{cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:520px){.key-figure{padding:.75rem}.key-layout{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.6rem}.panel-label{font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.4}.table-work{min-height:0}.key-figure :global(li){font-size:.74rem;line-height:1.45;padding:.4rem;gap:.15rem}.key-figure :global(li small){font-size:.7rem}.key-code{font-size:.72rem}.work-count,[data-explanation]{font-size:.82rem}select{font-size:.8rem}button{font-size:.8rem;padding:.4rem .6rem}}
</style>
